    {
      "comment": "Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Untapping an attacking creature doesn\u2019t cause it to stop attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "3d2ea1a3-72af-48bc-a8f1-98facc2eebd0",
      "published_at": "2011-01-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As Copperhorn Scout\u2019s ability resolves, you\u2019ll untap each other creature you control regardless of whether that creature was attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "3d2ea1a3-72af-48bc-a8f1-98facc2eebd0",
      "published_at": "2011-01-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To cast a fused split spell, pay both of its mana costs. While the spell is on the stack, its mana value is the total amount of mana in both costs.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When resolving a fused split spell with multiple targets, treat it as you would any spell with multiple targets. If all targets are illegal when the spell tries to resolve, the spell doesn't resolve and none of its effects happen. If at least one target is still legal at that time, the spell resolves, but an illegal target can't perform any actions or have any actions performed on it.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some split cards with fuse have two halves that are both multicolored. That card is multicolored no matter which half is cast, or if both halves are cast. It's also multicolored while not on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a player names a card, the player may name either half of a split card, but not both. A split card has the chosen name if one of its two names matches the chosen name.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you're casting a split card with fuse from any zone other than your hand, you can't cast both halves. You'll only be able to cast one half or the other.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you cast a split card with fuse from your hand without paying its mana cost, you can choose to use its fuse ability and cast both halves without paying their mana costs.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On the stack, a split spell that hasn't been fused has only that half's characteristics and mana value. The other half is treated as though it didn't exist.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a fused split spell resolves, follow the instructions of the left half first, then the instructions on the right half.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some split cards with fuse have two monocolor halves of different colors. If such a card is cast as a fused split spell, the resulting spell is multicolored. If only one half is cast, the spell is the color of that half. While not on the stack, such a card is multicolored.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature that comes under your control after Willing resolves won't have deathtouch or lifelink, because adding abilities does change a creature's characteristics.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Multiple instances of deathtouch or lifelink are redundant.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can choose the same object as the target of each half of a fused split spell, if appropriate.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature that comes under your control after Ready resolves will not be granted by this effect.",
      "oracle_id": "44c7c6bb-2592-4d7c-8485-1815093e70be",
      "published_at": "2013-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.",
      "oracle_id": "8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90",
      "published_at": "2012-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
